   "CLEANUP_BRANCH_INVALID": "WHAT: Cleanup run from wrong branch: {current_branch}.\nWHY: HAMMER require stable integration branch.\nHOW: Run from {default_branch}, staging, or testing branch.\nCONSEQUENCE: Cleanup blocked. OBEY BRANCH.",
   "WORKTREE_MERGE_CONFLICT": "WHAT: Merge conflict: {branch} with {default}.\nWHY: CONFLICT DETECTED during worktree sync.\nHOW: Resolution Steps:\n   1. Navigate to the worktree: 'cd $(tasks mount {task_id})'\n   2. Resolve the conflicts in the files indicated by 'git status'.\n   3. Commit the resolution:\n\n       git commit -m \"[{task_id}] Resolved merge conflict with {default} branch\"\n   4. Re-attempt the move:\n\n       ./hammer tasks move {task_id} TESTING\nCONSEQUENCE: Integration fail. OBEY RESOLUTION.",
   "CONFLICT_DETECTED": "WHAT: Merge conflicts detected in worktree '{branch}'.\nWHY: Code changes conflict with target branch.\nHOW:\n   1. Navigate to the worktree: 'cd $(tasks mount {task_id})'\n   2. Run: git status (to see conflicted files)\n   3. Resolve conflicts manually\n   4. Stage and commit: git add . && git commit -m 'Resolved conflicts'\n   5. Re-attempt the move.\nCONSEQUENCE: Promotion halted. RESOLVE CONFLICT.",
-  "GUARD_DUPLICATE_ID": "WHAT: Task ID {task_id} claimed by MULTIPLE branch.\nWHY: DUPLICATE ID. HAMMER cannot know which branch is the real task.\nHOW: Run 'hammer tasks doctor --fix' to reconcile — the guard never deletes branches itself. --force overrides (bypass is logged).\nCONSEQUENCE: Silent task identity corruption. REJECTED.",
-  "GUARD_DUPLICATE_REMOTE_ID": "WHAT: Task ID {task_id} claimed by MULTIPLE REMOTE branch.\nWHY: REMOTE DUPLICATE. Origin disagrees with itself about which task is real.\nHOW: Run 'hammer guard refresh --fetch', then 'hammer tasks doctor --fix' to reconcile. --force overrides (bypass is logged).\nCONSEQUENCE: Remote identity corruption. REJECTED.",
-  "GUARD_STATE_DUPLICATE": "WHAT: Task ID {task_id} live in MULTIPLE state folder.\nWHY: SAME ID IN TWO PLACES. HAMMER guess which one is real — guess is not authority.\nHOW: Run 'hammer guard scan' for the full list, then 'hammer tasks doctor --fix' to reconcile. --force overrides (bypass is logged).\nCONSEQUENCE: Corrupted state, silent divergence. REJECTED.",
-  "GUARD_BRANCH_NONCONFORMANT": "WHAT: Branch '{branch}' BREAK CONVENTION.\nWHY: HAMMER demand <id>-<type>-<slug>.\nHOW: Run 'hammer tasks doctor --fix' to correct metadata 'Br' to the folder name. --force overrides (bypass is logged).\nCONSEQUENCE: Guard cannot verify identity. REJECTED.",
+  "GUARD_DUPLICATE_ID": "WHAT: Task ID {task_id} is claimed by multiple branches.\nWHY: DUPLICATE ID. The correct branch is ambiguous, so doctor will not delete either one.\nHOW: Start fresh: recreate the task with a new ID, then run 'hammer tasks mount <new-id>'.\nCONSEQUENCE: Silent task identity corruption. REJECTED.",
+  "GUARD_DUPLICATE_REMOTE_ID": "WHAT: Task ID {task_id} is claimed by multiple remote branches.\nWHY: REMOTE DUPLICATE. Origin disagrees with itself about which task is real.\nHOW: Run 'hammer guard refresh --fetch', then start fresh: recreate the task with a new ID and run 'hammer tasks mount <new-id>'.\nCONSEQUENCE: Remote identity corruption. REJECTED.",
+  "GUARD_STATE_DUPLICATE": "WHAT: Task ID {task_id} exists in multiple state folders.\nWHY: SAME ID IN TWO PLACES. The correct folder is ambiguous, so doctor will not choose one.\nHOW: Start fresh: recreate the task with a new ID, then run 'hammer tasks mount <new-id>'.\nCONSEQUENCE: Corrupted state, silent divergence. REJECTED.",
+  "GUARD_BRANCH_NONCONFORMANT": "WHAT: A branch for task {task_id} breaks the naming convention.\nWHY: HAMMER demands <id>-<type>-<slug>, but renaming a live branch can strand unmerged work.\nHOW: Start fresh: recreate the task with a new ID, then run 'hammer tasks mount <new-id>'.\nCONSEQUENCE: Guard cannot verify identity. REJECTED.",
   "GUARD_BRANCH_MISSING": "WHAT: Task {task_id} has NO LOCAL BRANCH.\nWHY: {to_state} require the branch to exist and be pushed.\nHOW: Run 'hammer tasks mount {task_id}' to restore it, or move the task back to PROGRESSING.\nCONSEQUENCE: Work trapped locally. REJECTED.",
-  "GUARD_REMOTE_DIVERGENCE": "WHAT: Task {task_id} has NO LOCAL BRANCH; remote still tracks it.\nWHY: LOCAL WORK LOST. Origin holds a copy the local repo cannot see.\nHOW: Run 'hammer tasks mount {task_id}' to restore the branch from origin, then 'hammer tasks doctor --fix'. --force overrides (bypass is logged).\nCONSEQUENCE: Work invisible to this repo. REJECTED.",
+  "GUARD_REMOTE_DIVERGENCE": "WHAT: Task {task_id} has no local branch while remote branches still exist.\nWHY: LOCAL WORK LOST. Origin holds a copy the local repo cannot see.\nHOW: Run 'hammer tasks mount {task_id}' to restore the branch from origin. If the remote identity is ambiguous, recreate the task with a fresh ID and mount it.\nCONSEQUENCE: Work invisible to this repo. REJECTED.",
   "GUARD_WORKTREE_PATH_DRIFT": "WHAT: A task's worktree is not at <worktrees_base>/<branch>.\nWHY: Hammer owns worktree paths; a consumer resolving that task by name would read or write outside the registered worktree.\nHOW: Run 'hammer tasks mount <id>' to re-register, or 'hammer tasks doctor' for the full report. --force overrides (bypass is logged).\nCONSEQUENCE: Path resolution is ambiguous. REJECTED.",
   "GUARD_WORKTREE_MISSING_WORKTREE": "WHAT: A manifest worktree path is not a git worktree.\nWHY: The directory hammer registered is gone or was never created, so the task has no working directory.\nHOW: Run 'hammer tasks mount <id>' to recreate it. --force overrides (bypass is logged).\nCONSEQUENCE: The task has nowhere to build. REJECTED.",
-  "GUARD_WORKTREE_UNREGISTERED": "WHAT: A directory under .task-worktrees/ is not in the manifest.\nWHY: Nobody owns that path; anything resolving a task through it works outside hammer's control.\nHOW: Run 'hammer tasks doctor --fix' to remove unregistered directories, or move the work to the registered path.\nCONSEQUENCE: Phantom paths. REJECTED.",
-  "GUARD_WORKTREE_LOCAL_STORE": "WHAT: A registered task worktree contains its own .tasks directory.\nWHY: A worktree-local store is invisible to other tasks and can diverge from the central record.\nHOW: Inspect the reported directory, then remove or migrate it only after explicit confirmation.\nCONSEQUENCE: Divergent task records. REJECTED.",
-  "GUARD_WORKTREE_ORPHAN": "WHAT: Worktree for task {task_id} has NO MATCHING BRANCH.\nWHY: ORPHANED WORKTREE. It points at a branch that no longer exists.\nHOW: Run 'hammer tasks doctor --fix' to reconcile worktrees. --force overrides (bypass is logged).\nCONSEQUENCE: Dangling workspace. REJECTED.",
+  "GUARD_WORKTREE_UNREGISTERED": "WHAT: A directory under .task-worktrees/ is not in the manifest.\nWHY: Nobody owns that path; anything resolving a task through it works outside hammer's control.\nHOW: Move the work to the registered path, or recreate the task with a fresh ID and run 'hammer tasks mount <new-id>'.\nCONSEQUENCE: Phantom paths. REJECTED.",
+  "GUARD_WORKTREE_LOCAL_STORE": "WHAT: A registered task worktree contains its own .tasks directory.\nWHY: A worktree-local store is invisible to other tasks and can diverge from the central record.\nHOW: Inspect the reported directory, remove or migrate it only after explicit confirmation, then run 'hammer tasks mount <id>'.\nCONSEQUENCE: Divergent task records. REJECTED.",
+  "GUARD_WORKTREE_ORPHAN": "WHAT: Worktree for task {task_id} has no matching branch.\nWHY: ORPHANED WORKTREE. It points at a branch that no longer exists, and deleting it may discard unmerged work.\nHOW: Recreate the task with a fresh ID and run 'hammer tasks mount <new-id>'; preserve the old worktree until it is reviewed.\nCONSEQUENCE: Dangling workspace. REJECTED.",
   "GUARD_WORKTREE_MISSING": "WHAT: Task {task_id} has NO WORKTREE.\nWHY: {to_state} require a worktree for the task's branch.\nHOW: Run 'hammer tasks mount {task_id}' to create it. --force overrides (bypass is logged).\nCONSEQUENCE: Task cannot be worked on. REJECTED.",
   "GUARD_UNAVAILABLE": "WHAT: Guard CANNOT VERIFY task {task_id}.\nWHY: Cache corrupt or git subprocess failed. Guard fail closed — a silent pass is the bug this tool exists to kill.\nHOW: Run 'hammer guard rebuild' then retry. --force overrides and logs the bypass.\nCONSEQUENCE: Unverified transition. REJECTED.",
   "STORE_WRITE_FAIL": "WHAT: Git refused to stage or commit this task's store changes.\nWHY: The shared .tasks store is one repo used by every agent; a failed write means this update exists on disk but never reaches the record, and would be silently lost.\nHOW: Check for a stale .tasks/.git/index.lock or a broken store repo, then retry the checkpoint.\nCONSEQUENCE: Task record incomplete. Do not retry blindly.",
